From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 05:50:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: preserve Baldur panic wake and RX refill
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Keep the pinned TB323FU receive fixes on the unified ath12k datapath
for the Lenovo Y700 Gen5 (baldur).

The PCI bus wake-up callback calls mhi_device_get_sync(), which needs
the MHI thread.  A panic never schedules that thread, so the wake only
blocks the panicking CPU.  During a panic on lenovo,baldur, return
-EBUSY before the wake; the non-zero result also skips the matching
release, as in the original patch.  Every other machine keeps the
unconditional wake.

The receive code imports the original 0113 hunks as a whole, with no
rewritten strategy.  ath12k_dp_rx_bufs_replenish() tops up a deficit
larger than one eighth of the ring from the free descriptor list, and
the wifi7 reap path posts reaped buffers back even when no complete
MSDU was reaped.  Those two correctness fixes from the original are
intentionally common and are not machine-gated.  Allocation, mapping,
missing-descriptor, no-MSDU, top-up, watchdog and stall counters plus
the ring fill level are shown in device_dp_stats.

The deferrable one-second watchdog is new policy and only arms on
lenovo,baldur.  It quietly completes the initial fill from the
descriptor pool, then refills a half-empty ring and warns only when
nothing was reaped since the previous run.  Its timer_setup() runs on
every board because ath12k_dp_rx_free() calls the stop helper
unconditionally and that helper must find an initialized timer; it is
set up before any ath12k_dp_rx_alloc() failure path.  The helper uses
timer_shutdown_sync(), and ath12k_dp_cleanup() calls it before
ath12k_dp_cc_cleanup() frees the descriptors.

The generator imports the original 0058 and 0113 hunks onto the actual
unified preimages (7 files, 16 original hunks) and diffs the result at
U3; the hunk count in this patch comes from that diff.

Provenance: this project's Lenovo TB323FU tree at
11a25bf89b65fff48112a91a0b25bc247e7736d8, patches 0058 and 0113 by
Joonhoe Kim, rebased onto the unified datapath.  No sign-off is added.

---
 7 files changed, 198 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
---

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
  * Copyright (c) Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. and/or its subsidiaries.
  */
 
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/panic.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 
 #include "../pci.h"
@@ -63,6 +65,15 @@
 static int ath12k_wifi7_pci_bus_wake_up(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci = ath12k_pci_priv(ab);
+
+	/*
+	 * Panic context: the other CPUs are stopped and IRQs are off, so the M0
+	 * wake mhi_device_get_sync() waits for may never be seen. A non-zero
+	 * return also skips the matching release.
+	 */
+	if (panic_in_progress() &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+		return -EBUSY;
 
 	return mhi_device_get_sync(ab_pci->mhi_ctrl->mhi_dev);
 }
